1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--interactive-reading-with-audio","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/interactive-reading-with-audio","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/interactive-reading-with-audio","sourceHash":"febf7aef025c1c4d2eaebe7a98390fc36fb693c2f25f4d2a40145eba820f6c05","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:12.202Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Interactive Reading with Audio","zh":"互动式伴音阅读"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Interactive Reading with Audio is the core immersion activity for Phases 1-2. You're reading target-language text while simultaneously listening to matching audio, and you're stopping to look things up and work through understanding.","zh":"互动式伴音阅读是第 1 至第 2 阶段的核心沉浸活动。你一边阅读目标语言文本，一边同时听对应的音频，并不时停下来查询内容、逐步理清含义。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=10101-interactive-reading-with-audio&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; Interactive Reading with Audio tutorial and tool recommendations</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=10101-interactive-reading-with-audio&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; 互动式伴音阅读教程与工具推荐</a>"}},{"id":"what-it-looks-like","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What It Looks Like","zh":"具体是什么样"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The most common setup: watching a TV show or video with target-language subtitles. You pause frequently, read the subtitle, try to understand the sentence, look up unknown words, then continue. You're getting three channels of input at once — visual context (what's happening on screen), text (the subtitles), and audio (what's being said).","zh":"最常见的做法是：观看带有目标语言字幕的电视节目或视频。你会频繁暂停，阅读字幕，尝试理解句子，查询生词，然后继续播放。这样，你会同时通过三个通道获得输入——视觉语境（屏幕上正在发生的事情）、文本（字幕）和音频（说话内容）。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Other setups: reading a transcript while listening to a podcast, reading a book while listening to the audiobook, or using a reader app that pairs text with audio.","zh":"其他做法包括：边听播客边阅读文字稿、边听有声书边阅读书籍，或使用能将文本与音频配对的阅读应用。"}},{"id":"why-three-channels-matter","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why Three Channels Matter","zh":"为什么三个通道很重要"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Each channel helps compensate for what you don't know:","zh":"每个通道都能帮助弥补你尚未掌握的部分："}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Visual context</strong> helps you guess the meaning of words from the situation","zh":"<strong>视觉语境</strong>帮助你根据情境猜测词义"},{"en":"<strong>Text</strong> lets you see word boundaries clearly and look things up","zh":"<strong>文本</strong>让你清楚看见词语边界，并方便查询内容"},{"en":"<strong>Audio</strong> trains your ear to associate sounds with the words you're reading","zh":"<strong>音频</strong>训练你的耳朵，把声音与正在阅读的词语联系起来"}]},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This combination makes content much more comprehensible than any single channel alone. A sentence you might not understand from audio alone becomes clear when you can also read it and see what's happening on screen.","zh":"这种组合让内容比仅使用任何单一通道都更容易理解。一个只听音频时可能无法理解的句子，在你同时读到文字并看到屏幕上发生的事情后，就会变得清晰。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=10101-interactive-reading-with-audio&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; Interactive Reading with Audio tutorial and tool recommendations</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?item=10101-interactive-reading-with-audio&amp;type=activity\">-&gt; 互动式伴音阅读教程与工具推荐</a>"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"技巧"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Choose content where you can follow the story even when you miss individual sentences","zh":"选择这样的内容：即使漏掉个别句子，你仍然能够跟上故事情节"},{"en":"Auto-pause (pausing after each subtitle line) is helpful for beginners","zh":"自动暂停（在每行字幕结束后暂停）对初学者很有帮助"},{"en":"The process is slow at first — a 20-minute episode might take an hour. This is normal.","zh":"一开始，这个过程会很慢——一集 20 分钟的节目可能需要一小时。这很正常。"},{"en":"As your comprehension improves, you'll pause less and eventually transition toward freeflow","zh":"随着理解能力提升，你暂停的次数会越来越少，并最终逐渐转向顺畅式沉浸"},{"en":"Slice-of-life dramas are ideal starting content because they use everyday language with high visual context","zh":"日常生活类剧集是理想的入门内容，因为它们使用日常语言，并提供丰富的视觉语境"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Interactive Reading with Audio begins in Phase 1A and remains a key activity through Phase 2.","zh":"互动式伴音阅读从第 1A 阶段开始，并在整个第 2 阶段一直是关键活动。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
